User Service Agreement
1. About Us
Thank you for choosing to use our product.
This User Service Agreement is a valid agreement entered into between Liufangzhiwu and users (hereinafter referred to as you) regarding the use of our product.

2. Scope, Purpose, and Confirmation of the Agreement
This User Service Agreement, its supplementary agreements, and any separate agreements or rules displayed on the pages, as well as operation tips (collectively referred to as this Agreement), are the terms on which we provide product services to you. They are inseparable and must be observed together.
Please read all contents of this Agreement carefully, especially the bolded parts.
If you have any questions about this Agreement or the page prompts, please do not proceed to the next step. If you use our product or services, you will be deemed to have read and agreed to be bound by this Agreement.
If you do not agree with any part of this Agreement, or cannot accurately understand its terms, please stop using the product and do not proceed with any follow-up actions.

3. Requirements for Using This Service
3.1 You must have full civil capacity to use our product. If you have no civil capacity or limited civil capacity, please inform your guardian, read this Agreement under your guardian's guidance, and use our product only after obtaining your guardian's consent;
3.2 You expressly state and warrant that you have sufficient legal rights or authorization to sign and perform this Agreement; your signing and performance of this Agreement will not conflict with or cause a breach of any other agreement or arrangement you are required to perform;
3.3 If the laws of your country or region exclude all or part of this Agreement, you shall immediately stop using our product. Otherwise, your continued use of our product will be deemed as your agreement to bear the relevant legal risks or liabilities.

5. Rules for User Conduct
5.1 Any actions performed or instructions issued using your identity credentials shall be deemed to have been made by you. You shall be responsible for all consequences arising from the use of your identity credentials (including but not limited to signing agreements, publishing information, paying for goods and services, and disclosing information). Any risks and losses caused by your account, password, or other information being impersonated, stolen, or illegally used due to reasons attributable to you shall be borne by you;
5.2 When using our product, please fill in and verify your personal information carefully to ensure it is true, accurate, complete, and valid;
5.3 Please consider your actual needs and carefully review information such as the Privacy Policy and User Agreement before confirming and choosing to use our product and services;
5.4 You acknowledge and agree that if you suffer any financial loss or consequences due to input errors, improper operations, wrong selections, or similar situations on your part, you shall bear them yourself.

6. Disclaimer
Before using our product, you should have a certain understanding of the risks that may exist in e-commerce and network services. Failures, interruptions, or delays in our services caused by network failures, system inspection, maintenance or instability, hacker attacks, technical adjustments or failures by power departments, banks, or other reasons do not constitute a breach by Liufangzhiwu, but Liufangzhiwu will make every effort to restore normal services. As a technical service platform, Liufangzhiwu provides services on an as-is basis only. To the extent permitted by law, Liufangzhiwu shall not be liable for service interruptions, delays, or obstacles caused by the following circumstances:
(1) Damage caused by computer viruses, Trojans or other malicious programs, or hacker attacks;
(2) Failures in your or a third party's computer software, system, hardware, network, or communication lines;
(3) Improper operations by you, including but not limited to submitting incorrect account or personal information, or program errors;
(4) Other circumstances beyond Liufangzhiwu's control or reasonable foresight.

7. Prohibited Conduct by Users
When using this software, you must comply with laws and regulations and may not use the services provided by this software to engage in illegal or non-compliant acts, including but not limited to:
(1) Publishing, transmitting, disseminating, or storing content that endangers national security and unity, undermines social stability, violates public order and good customs, is insulting, defamatory, obscene, violent, or otherwise violates national laws and regulations;
(2) Publishing, transmitting, disseminating, or storing content that infringes the legitimate rights and interests of others, such as intellectual property rights and trade secrets;
(3) Maliciously fabricating facts or concealing the truth to mislead or deceive others;
(4) Publishing, transmitting, or disseminating advertising information or spam;
(5) Other acts prohibited by laws and regulations.
If you violate this clause and cause any damage to any third party, you shall bear sole responsibility. If Liufangzhiwu suffers losses as a result, you shall also compensate for them in full.

8. Revisions to This Agreement
You may review the relevant terms in the latest version of this software. Once published, the updated terms will replace the original terms, and we will promptly post changes to this Agreement on the service page. If revisions to this Agreement materially affect you or significantly restrict your access to or use of the service, we will notify you within a reasonable period before the changes take effect. For revisions made to meet security, legal, or regulatory requirements, we may not be able to meet the foregoing advance notice period, but we will notify you as soon as possible.
After the terms of this Agreement are changed, if you do not accept the revised agreement, please stop using the service immediately; if you continue to access or use the service, you will be deemed to have accepted the revised agreement.

9. Governing Law and Jurisdiction
The formation, execution, interpretation, and dispute resolution of this Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China.
You agree that the place of signing of this Agreement is Hongshan District, Wuhan City, Hubei Province, China.
If any dispute arises during the performance of this Agreement, both parties shall first resolve it through negotiation. If negotiation fails, both parties shall bring a lawsuit before the people's court with jurisdiction at the place where the Agreement is signed.

Effective Date: 2025.8.20
